    "turn_text": "So for today's let's get blunt. I'm going to get very blunt about the double standard that exists in so many spaces in our world, in our society, in the international community, agencies, politics, etc. And I'm going to focus on the current issue or issues in Ukraine starting with Ukraine and what is happening or at least what we are being told is happening on the surface because as most of us know there's so much underneath the surface that is not reported by mainstream media, commercial media. But under surface, we're told that Russia is about to invade Ukraine. And if so, the US and other European nations will intervene, etc. When many brilliant analysts are saying that this is really Not the case Russia if if anything is going to Sort of in quotes on one city that it feels as part of the old sort of Russian Left over from the Soviet era that it wants to reclaim And that this is really about NATO wanting to flex its muscles and say Here, we de-escalated, you know, a potential war. We are very relevant, et cetera. And it's also a way for Putin to say, don't sort of come into my neighborhood and honor the original pact that was made when NATO was created. Anyways, But that's not even the point. The point I'm trying to make is this. Based on a potential, okay, so quote unquote, potential attack on Ukraine. The U.S. and a lot of European countries, but let's just focus on the U.S. with President Biden and Secretary Blinken, our State Department, and many politicians are just ready to go to war as if we're going to start World War III to save lives, quote unquote. But here's the thing. Nobody's life is more important than others. Or at least it shouldn't be in an ideal world. But here's the thing. Year and a half ago, in 2020, rogue dictator terrorist nations of Azerbaijan and Turkey, with hired mercenaries that were ISIS, as well as Syrian, Libyan, and Pakistani mercenaries, orchestrated a genocidal attack and ethnic cleansing on the Armenians of the Autonomous Republic of Artsakh, also known as the Garmel-Rabakh, and massacred 5,000 Armenians in 44 days. But most people didn't even hear about it. There was a deafening silence in just throughout the world. You'd have to really look to find some sort of a statement from someone. Of course, many members of Congress who had the humanity, who knew what was happening, they spoke up. But I'm talking about U.S. as a whole Secretary Blinken. and President Biden, all you heard were toxic, both side-ism, sort of with this robotic statements that they made where they did false balance on what was happening. So my question is, why is it that Armenia, which is not that far away from Ukraine, they're both Eastern European countries, Armenia is in the South Caucasus, Ukraine is in the greater Caucasus. Why is it that Armenian's lives didn't matter? Why is it that even a quarter, even a tenth of this pandemonium wasn't created when this was happening in 2020 and we were killing ourselves trying to get somebody's attention and nothing was happening. And remember, Turkey, who engineered and helped Azerbaijan to plan and orchestrate and supply weapons to Azerbaijan to do all of this, is a member of NATO. And yet they walked away with impunity. So is this a part of NATO's values to allow its members to orchestrate ethnic cleansing and massacres? And by the way, this is still happening. Armenia and Artsakh are under threat as we speak by Azerbaijan and Turkey. And yet because Armenia is a tiny nation of 3 million and Artsakh is, well, after two thirds of its population that became refugees is left with maybe about 50 or 60,000 people with not much of natural resources to offer to the world. It's being ignored. And of course, whatever natural resources Artsach has is now under occupation of Azerbaijan, gold mines, as well as water resources. So, why did you double standard? And I'm saying this as a Democrat. I'm saying this as a progressive. I'm saying this as someone who voted for President Biden. But you've got to call them out. I don't care if they're a Democrat or Republican or independent or what they are. The bottom line is, why? Why didn't you, with a single phone call? And I understand that at the time this happened, President Biden wasn't the president. It was Trump. But, of course, Trump forgot about him. I mean, he was, you know, pals with Erdogan and Aliyah, and, you know, likely he gave him a green light to what they did. But now, now President Biden can do a lot more. President Biden... Lived at Section 907 of the Freedom Act and gave Azerbaijan a hundred million dollars of military aid just last year. And this is after Azerbaijan invaded Artsakh and killed 5,000 people. So we've got to call them out. We've got to get blunt about these things and say, why is this really happening? What is the real reason that Ukraine has become this pandemonium? Is it about energy? Is it about sort of a cold war era type of a conflict between Russia and US? Or is this just NATO flexing its muscles? So let's get blunt. Let's get",
